onstraint at $100M is not capital........
It is decision velocity


At this stage, most CEOs believe the next unlock is capital, talent, or sys=
tems.

The constraint is usually decision velocity.

What it looks like:
=E2=80=A2 Too many decisions routed through a small number of leaders
=E2=80=A2 Lack of clarity on decision ownership
=E2=80=A2 More meetings but slower outcomes
=E2=80=A2 Teams waiting instead of executing

This is one of the most common entry points for me as a fractional.
When leadership bandwidth becomes the bottleneck, the business slows.

In several companies I have worked with:
=E2=80=A2 Decision cycle time increased 20 to 40 percent
=E2=80=A2 Key initiatives stalled without clear ownership
=E2=80=A2 Leadership teams became reactive instead of proactive

The fix is not more meetings.
It is clarity in decision rights and operating rhythm.

Once that is installed:
=E2=80=A2 Execution accelerates
=E2=80=A2 Accountability increases
=E2=80=A2 Leaders regain capacity

Growth requires more people.

Scale requires faster decisions.

Question for presidents and CEOs
Where in your business are decisions waiting longer than they should?<butto=
