 EBITDA Killer #5...... Margin Blind Spots





One of the most dangerous EBITDA leaks I see in retail isn=E2=80=99t operat=
ional.
It=E2=80=99s visibility.

Specifically=E2=80=A6 margin visibility.

Many companies track revenue extremely well.
Fewer truly understand where profit is coming from.

What I see often:
=E2=80=A2 Certain SKUs growing quickly but carrying lower margins
=E2=80=A2 Cost inputs shifting (freight, materials, labor)
=E2=80=A2 Pricing not keeping pace
=E2=80=A2 Promotions eroding profitability more than expected

On paper, the business looks like it=E2=80=99s growing.
Underneath, margin is quietly deteriorating.

This is what I call a margin blind spot.

Once companies implement true pricing and margin analytics at the SKU and c=
hannel level, the picture changes quickly:
=E2=80=A2 Unprofitable growth becomes visible
=E2=80=A2 Pricing decisions become intentional
=E2=80=A2 Promotional strategy becomes disciplined
=E2=80=A2 Product mix improves

And EBITDA improves; often faster than expected.

Not because the business changed overnight.
Because leadership could finally see clearly.

Revenue tells you how fast you=E2=80=99re growing.
Margin tells you how well you=E2=80=99re growing.

Question for founders:
If you looked SKU by SKU today=E2=80=A6
